    "tier": "community",
    "url": "https://hn.algolia.com/api/v1/items/33001391",
    "excerpt": "I just use SMTP for this (with FastMail). FastMail is not really intended for [transactional emails at scale] as the limits and the like don't really scale to large services, but overall it works well enough (you can create an 'app password' which can only access SMTP).",
    "fetchedAt": "2026-09-07T03:14:46.572Z"
  },
  {
    "id": "fastmail-comm-12",
    "tier": "community",
    "url": "https://hn.algolia.com/api/v1/items/12247401",
    "excerpt": "FastMail is an upgrade from GMail. It's good enough, that after swearing never to pay for a webmail service at one time, I remain a paying customer of FastMail after 10+ years.",
